    <!--
      The tutorial.

      Four screens, shown once, skippable from the first. It exists because the best
      thing in the app — a ready-made breakdown for the kind of thing you are planning —
      sits behind the + button, and a first-time user has no reason to believe it is
      there. An empty list that says "tap + to create your first budget" sells nothing.
    -->
    <string name="tour_skip">Skip</string>
    <string name="tour_next">Next</string>
    <string name="tour_done">Create my first budget</string>
    <string name="tour_replay">Show the tutorial again</string>
    <string name="tour_replay_sub">Four screens on what the app does and how to use it</string>

    <string name="tour_1_title">A budget is a pot of money</string>
    <string name="tour_1_body">A salary month. A wedding. A savings target. You give it a total, split that total into categories, and log what you spend against them.\n\nThat is the whole app. Everything else is a view of those three things.</string>

    <string name="tour_2_title">Never start from a blank page</string>
    <string name="tour_2_body">Tell SapioSpend what you are planning and it offers breakdowns built for it — a monthly salary, a traditional wedding, a conference, a savings goal.\n\nThe percentages are a starting point. Drag them around until they look like your life.</string>

    <string name="tour_3_title">Log it as it happens</string>
    <string name="tour_3_body">Record the full cost, then say whether it is paid, part paid on a deposit, or not paid yet. SapioSpend keeps what you owe apart from what you have actually spent.\n\nPut the widget on your home screen and logging a spend takes two taps.</string>

    <string name="tour_4_title">Know where you stand</string>
    <string name="tour_4_body">Planned against actual, category by category. What you can still safely spend each day. A warning at 80%% of the total, and again if you go over.\n\nIt all stays on your phone. No account, no sign-in, nothing uploaded.</string>

